      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T03:22:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s expected (but not certain) that this will be optional in Compat as well. Not sure what Dawn\u0027s implementation status of that restriction is though.\nThe restriction is exposed via a limit:\nhttps://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/compatibility-mode.md#19-introduce-new-maxstoragebuffersinfragmentstage-and-maxstoragetexturesinfragmentstage-limits\n\nNot a huge deal; the only problem is that some vulkan devices could be considered unsupported when they should actually be supported. Could just file a bug for it and add a TODO maybe.",
      "revId": "750052550f1edc87cefca5be66d124e232ce7dc7",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f82de7c_675b88f4",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/DeviceVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 427,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T16:15:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just want to be sure I understand, if maxStorageBuffersInFragmentStage and maxStorageBuffersInFragmentStage are both zero (which implies we\u0027re in compat mode since that\u0027s not allowed in core) then we can leave this feature disabled since there will be no storage buffer/textures used in the fragment stage?\n\nDoes maxStorageBuffersInFragmentStage and maxStorageBuffersInFragmentStage apply only for writeable buffers? It seems like non-writeable buffers are still allowed in the fragment stage.\n\n\u003e fragmentStoresAndAtomics specifies whether storage buffers and images support stores and atomic operations in the fragment shader stage. If this feature is not enabled, all storage image, storage texel buffer, and storage buffer variables used by the fragment stage in shader modules must be decorated with the NonWritable decoration (or the readonly memory qualifier in GLSL).\n\nI\u0027ll file a bug though since this is more subtle.",
      "parentUuid": "1f101dc8_a73cfa95",
      "revId": "750052550f1edc87cefca5be66d124e232ce7dc7",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "486176ee_7344dd94",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/DeviceVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 427,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T22:08:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Does maxStorageBuffersInFragmentStage and maxStorageBuffersInFragmentStage apply only for writeable buffers? It seems like non-writeable buffers are still allowed in the fragment stage.\n\nNo, it applies to readonly buffers as well. These limits come from GLES primarily, which doesn\u0027t make a distinction between readonly and writable.",
      "parentUuid": "7f82de7c_675b88f4",
      "revId": "750052550f1edc87cefca5be66d124e232ce7dc7",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87ed708b_a501e0ef",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/DeviceVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 429,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T03:22:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure but I think this one is also optional. We did restrict sample_index:\nhttps://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/compatibility-mode.md#7-disallow-sample_mask-and-sample_index-builtins-in-wgsl\nand interpolation modes:\nhttps://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/compatibility-mode.md#11-disallow-linear-and-sample-interpolation-options\nso when fragmentStoresAndAtomics\u003dfalse we might not need this either.",
      "revId": "750052550f1edc87cefca5be66d124e232ce7dc7",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
